  "details": "Adding instance kicks through an API endpoint would be a VERY useful feature for group instance moderation, allowing moderators to kick users from an instance without having to actually being present in the lobby using custom tools.\n\nI have seen so many instances where a moderator wasn't present and had to be called to get on to take care of a user breaking the rules, this happens a lot in some 24/7 lobbies.\n\nKick through API would also open up so many opportunities for community tools.\n\nI personally made a discord bot to help my mod team with the moderation of my instance, notifying of when possible ban evaders join the lobby, which is a problem a regularly deal with. One specific user makes almost 10 accounts a day to do this, being able to kick and ban from the instance through my discord bot would help us a lot with that.\n\nBut I could also see this work as an instance close feature for events, where it also forces everyone out of the lobby instead of only preventing people from joining for example.\n\nThere are a lot of possibilities with this, and I don't see this hurting anyone as long as only group moderators can use this.\n\nBans through API already exist, but they unfortunately don't kick the users from the instance. Meaning that you can ban someone using it while they're still in the lobby, and it wont get rid of them.\n\nThis was reported here:  https://feedback.vrchat.com/bug-reports/p/real-time-enforcement-issue-with-group-bans-via-website-api\n\nThe ideal fix to that would of course be to straight up also add instance kick functionality to the API.",
